WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.430
Hi, my name's Jordan Achay.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.440
I'm a groundskeeper in
professional football.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.852
Today, I'm going to guide
you through the process

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.537
of deep cleaning and
preparing an NFL field

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:22.645
for the Super Bowl.

00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:27.503
I started groundskeeping
for the Los Angeles

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:30.840
Memorial Coliseum in USC in 2016.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.340
From there, I went on
to SoFi Stadium in 2021.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.770
When I found out the Super Bowl
was coming to SoFi Stadium,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.270
it was very exciting to
know that I would have

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.660
the opportunity to be a
part of such a big event.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.060
When you're working in
a higher-scale setting,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.470
such as professional football,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.910
there are a lot more fine details

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.880
that go into all the
planning and the execution

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.655
when it comes to events and preparation

00:00:52.655 --> 00:00:53.805
as well as cleanup.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.310
The first step to preparing
the field for the Super Bowl

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.863
is removing the paint
from the previous game.

00:01:02.987 --> 00:01:04.710
The machine that we use to clean the field

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.140
is called a P-Rex, and what it does is,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.125
there are brushes with
very strong bristles

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:13.380
in a circular shape that go
down and scrub the paint off

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.173
after we spray down a solution.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.320
We have somebody driving
each and every one,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.030
and there are a few out there on the field

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.336
after the game ends.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.940
Once the paint is starting
to break up and be liquid,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.753
there's a vacuum that sucks
the excess paint into a tank.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.220
These machines have something
that sprays the tires

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.900
in order to remove the paint from them

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.810
so there's no tracking, and that way

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.910
we don't get paint in spots
that we don't want it.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.930
When it's time to get new
brushes and drain the tank,

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.140
then we drive into our wash station.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.393
We start the cleaning
process of the P-Rex.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.080
So, right now we're
removing the used brushes,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.060
spraying them off to
get all the paint off,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.640
storing them off to the
side so they can dry,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.160
and putting a new brush onto each P-Rex

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.710
in order to send it back out
and start cleaning again.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.270
It's time to fill up the tanks with water

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.130
and the paint-removing solution.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.380
We dump the tank that filters the rubber

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.570
out of the used paint,

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.243
and then from there we
dispose of the paint.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.126
So, the brushes on the P-Rex

00:02:23.126 --> 00:02:26.160
go down onto the turf and spin,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.040
as well as the operator drives the machine

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.500
back and forth in order to remove paint

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.590
from a certain area
mixed with the solution.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.150
I'd say the removal process can take

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.920
anywhere from two to four hours.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.820
We just keep going

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.130
until we don't see any
more paint on the field,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:44.255
and it's good to go and
ready for the next paint day.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.354
Now that we've finished removing

00:02:48.354 --> 00:02:49.911
all the paint from the field

00:02:49.911 --> 00:02:52.144
and it's clear to go
for the next paint day,

00:02:52.144 --> 00:02:54.893
we can start the process of painting.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.920
The process of painting for the Super Bowl

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.540
is different from any other game

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.950
because there is a whole other crew

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.342
that is also involved in the painting.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.180
So, the preparation
process for the Super Bowl

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.963
starts at least two weeks
ahead of the actual game.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.300
When painting for the Super
Bowl, there are different logos

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.310
that we've never used
before, new stencils.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.190
So we have to map out
where everything goes

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.352
and measure the spots for
these specific stencils,

00:03:26.352 --> 00:03:29.430
and that may be in a spot on the field

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.505
that has never been painted before.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.510
So, while we paint these logos,

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.780
we want the lines and
edges to be straight.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.982
We have straight edges,

00:03:43.982 --> 00:03:46.950
and we have flimsy boards that can be set

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.160
on specific spots in
order to prevent the paint

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.635
from getting into a spot that
it's not supposed to be in.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.730
So, after we get done painting,

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.410
it's time to clean the equipment.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.990
These boards we take to the back washroom,

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.693
and we use solution to get the paint off.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.730
So, this paint board is caked
in paint with multiple layers,

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:11.340
so we need to spray, scrape,

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.243
and use solution until we get it all off.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.070
Paint does splatter,
paint does get everywhere,

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.010
so we need to make sure the
entire machine is clean.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.770
Takes a little while in order
to get all the paint off,

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.006
but once it's clean, it looks
great and it's worth it.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.010
So, it's important to clean the
paint machines because, one,

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.320
you want to take care of
the equipment that you use,

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.030
make sure that it can last as long

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.860
as you would like it to last.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.960
You don't want paint
buildup in certain areas

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.395
on the machine because then that can

00:04:53.395 --> 00:04:56.512
start to limit the
functionality of the machine.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.150
Watching the confetti rain
down on the field is surreal,

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.940
and I would not trade that
feeling for the world,

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.960
until I realized that we were
going to have to clean it up.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.118
So, to clean this confetti up,

00:05:14.118 --> 00:05:15.977
we're using as many blowers as we have

00:05:15.977 --> 00:05:17.550
in order to bring all the confetti

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.200
to one side of the field in one area

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.230
so we can shovel it up and
pour it in the trash can,

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.060
remove, and just keep doing it over

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.060
and over and over until it's all gone.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.900
Once the confetti is cleaned up,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.670
we use a machine called the LitterKat

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.803
to remove excess debris from the field.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.340
The LitterKat is part of
our daily maintenance,

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.921
but it is important to use
it after the games as well

00:05:40.921 --> 00:05:43.746
because there are a
lot of pieces of debris

00:05:43.746 --> 00:05:45.462
that get onto the field.

00:05:45.462 --> 00:05:46.770
The first part of the machine

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.050
is going to suck up the lighter debris,

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:52.770
and the back end of
the machine is a magnet

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.203
that will remove all the
metal from the field.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.370
When we're removing the
debris out of the LitterKat,

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.610
we tend to find a lot of
screws from players' helmets,

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.100
small pieces of metal,
small pieces of plastic,

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.353
as well as sunflower-seed shells.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.016
My favorite thing about
being a groundskeeper

00:06:12.016 --> 00:06:14.700
is the team aspect. I work
with a lot of great people.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.500
It's fun to be around them

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.967
and to work towards a common goal

00:06:17.967 --> 00:06:20.850
of making sure a playing
surface is working great

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.640
for something of such magnitude.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.140
Being a part of the Super Bowl process

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.150
is something that I wouldn't
trade for the world.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.590
It was a surreal feeling,

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.573
and I'm excited to watch
this year's Super Bowl.

